.TH HTTPSERVER 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
httpserver \- serve a directory over HTTP or HTTPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B httpserver
.I dir
.RI [ port ]
.RB [ \-\-tls ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B httpserver
starts a simple HTTP file server rooted at
.IR dir .
All local IPv4 addresses and the listening URL are printed to standard output
when the server starts.
.PP
The server handles the following HTTP methods:
.RS
.TP
.B GET
Returns the file at the requested path, or an HTML directory listing if the
path is a directory.
If a directory contains an
.B index.html
file it is served instead of the listing.
A directory path without a trailing slash redirects (301) to the path with one.
.TP
.B HEAD
Same as GET but omits the response body.
.TP
.B OPTIONS
Returns 204 with an
.B Allow
header listing the supported methods.
.RE
.PP
Path traversal (
.BR ..
components) is rejected with 404.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I port
TCP port to listen on.
Defaults to
.B 8080
(plain HTTP) or
.B 8443
(with
.BR \-\-tls ).
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Enable HTTPS using a self-signed certificate generated at build time.
Requires the binary to be compiled with the
.B embedded-tls
feature.
.SH MIME TYPES
Content-Type is inferred from file extension:
.BR .html / .htm " → text/html,"
.BR .css " → text/css,"
.BR .js " → text/javascript,"
.BR .json " → application/json,"
.BR .png " → image/png,"
.BR .jpg / .jpeg " → image/jpeg,"
.BR .gif " → image/gif,"
.BR .svg " → image/svg+xml,"
.BR .txt " → text/plain,"
.BR .pdf " → application/pdf."
All other extensions use
.BR application/octet-stream .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "httpserver ./public"
Serve the
.B ./public
directory on port 8080.
.TP
.B "httpserver ./public 3000"
Serve on port 3000.
.TP
.B "httpserver ./public --tls"
Serve on port 8443 over HTTPS.
.TP
.B "httpserver ./public 9443 --tls"
Serve on port 9443 over HTTPS.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Server exited cleanly (unlikely in normal operation).
.TP
.B 1
Argument error or failure to bind the requested port.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1),
.BR hako (1)
